hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"977","Narrated to us Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala, narrated to us Sufyan bin Uyaynah, narrated to us Al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, H. Saeed bin Abd narrated to us. Al-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi, Ali bin Khashram, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Zuhri, and Ahmad bin Abdah. Ali said: Ibn Uyaynah told us And the others said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he heard Anas bin Malik, and this is the hadith of Abdul-Jabbar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell.” And he was delivered from a mare, and his right flank coltted, so we went in to return him, and the time for prayer came, and he prayed with us, sitting.”"
